+
+## Plain-text extraction
+
+With the matching libansilove text-export patch installed:
+
+    ansilove -x file.ans > file.txt
+
+`-x` exports the final character layout using the same decoders as PNG output.
+Only printable ASCII (bytes 32 through 126) and line feeds are emitted. Extended
+characters and control glyphs become spaces, so neighboring words stay separate.
+Characters whose foreground equals their background also become spaces. Leading
+and trailing blank rows and trailing spaces are removed; internal spacing remains.
+No PNG, progress messages, timing, or SAUCE metadata are written. `-q` is unnecessary.
+
+Supported inputs are ANSI, PCBoard, BIN, ADF, IDF, Tundra, and XBin. IDF, Tundra,
+and XBin signatures are recognized regardless of filename extension. Valid SAUCE
+width hints are used automatically; `-c` overrides them. `-t` can force the format.
+`-x` cannot be combined with `-o` or `-s`; redirect stdout to save a file.
+
+The output reflects the final image, so animations ending in a clear screen yield
+empty text. It is not OCR: lettering drawn with blocks or remapped custom-font
+characters cannot be recovered as words. Avatar is unsupported. ANSI positioning
+and erasure retain the existing renderer's behavior. An extraction is limited to
+64 MiB of character-grid storage.
